osu file format v14

// hitsound resolution cases that live on a SLIDER's nodes: per-node sounds
// and per-node banks on a repeating slider, the tail resolving under whatever
// point its own (leniency-shifted) time lands in, and the tick sample the
// slider's own hitsound produces.
//
// beat length 500 with SliderMultiplier 1.4 gives 140 px/beat; every slider
// below is 140 px per span, i.e. exactly 500 ms per span, so the node times
// are whole beats and it is obvious which sample point each one falls under.

[General]
AudioFilename: audio.mp3
Mode: 0

[Metadata]
Title:Sample Nodes
Artist:fixture
Creator:fixture
Version:Nodes
BeatmapID:0
BeatmapSetID:-1

[Difficulty]
HPDrainRate:5
CircleSize:4
OverallDifficulty:8
ApproachRate:9
SliderMultiplier:1.4
SliderTickRate:1

[TimingPoints]
0,500,4,1,0,100,1,0
3200,-100,4,3,0,40,0,0
6000,-100,4,2,0,90,0,0

[HitObjects]
// three spans (two repeats) => four nodes. edgeSounds names a different
// addition per node and edgeSets a different bank per node, so head, repeat 0,
// repeat 1 and tail must each resolve to their own sound
32,192,1000,2,0,L|172:192,3,140,2|4|8|2,1:1|2:2|3:3|2:0,0:0:0:0:
// no edgeSounds/edgeSets at all: every node falls back to the object's own
// hitsound, which is what PopulateNodeSamples copies in
32,240,3000,2,4,L|172:240,1,140,,,0:0:0:0:
// this slider STARTS under the normal/volume 100 point and ENDS under the
// drum/volume 40 one at 3200: its head keeps normal while its tail takes drum,
// which is the CONTROL_POINT_LENIENCY case -- each node resolves at its own
// time, not at the object's
32,288,3100,2,0,L|172:288,1,140,,,0:0:0:0:
// a slider hitsounded onto drum: its ticks must inherit drum, never the
// normal bank the nodes below would otherwise suggest
32,336,4000,2,0,L|312:336,1,280,0|0,3:3|1:1,3:3:0:0:
// a long slider that CROSSES the 6000 sample point, with ticks on both sides
// of it. lazer resolves a slider's own samples -- the ones its tick sample is
// derived from -- at start + LENIENCY + 1, so every tick here takes the bank
// and volume in force at 5000. this is the one case where the decoder the
// engine wraps disagrees with lazer (see formats::beatmap::convert_samples and
// TODO.md), so it is carried deliberately rather than avoided
32,48,5000,2,0,L|312:48,1,560,,,0:0:0:0:
